            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**The first map refused to divide 19 reported destroyed by 115 mapped. That\nrefusal still stands.**\n\nInside the extent there are\n**171** bridges\nand\n**43**\ndestroyed. HOT's separate assessment looked at 59 and called 39 washed out.\n\nTwo counts, not one. Neither can be held against the reported 19, which still\ncarries no stretch of river.\n\n**On the map:** every bridge, dark red where destroyed\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The bridges, and whether the numbers can be compared yet"
        }
      }
    },
