        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "fig-reflight.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Copernicus graded 3,816 buildings across four areas. Then\nthey flew one of those areas again, two days later.**\n\n![The same ground graded twice, two days apart](attachment:fig-reflight.png)\n\nSame ground, same team, same method. The second look found\n**653 more buildings\ndestroyed** than the first, a rise of\n36%.\n\nNothing on the ground changed between those two dates. What changed was how long\nanyone had been looking. **An early damage count is a floor, not a total**, and\nthis is that stated as a measurement rather than as a caution.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Looking again changed the count"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000009": {
      "name": "Four counts of the same thing",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 10.8,
        "extent": [
          9430547.08159633,
          3217447.3413577504,
          9529588.965596877,
          3290411.7080283663
