          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Every layer here is a published product. Every feature carries its source,\nlicence, retrieval date and a tier saying what it can support.**\n\n**Observed**\n\n- Flood extent, damage mapping, bridges, schools and mapping project areas:\n  [Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/hot_flood_npl),\n  rebuilt from OpenStreetMap, ODbL 1.0.\n- Damage grading and not-analysed ground:\n  [Copernicus EMS, EMSR927](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/npl-flood-emsr927),\n  © 2026 European Union.\n- Flood extent, detachment zone and barrier lakes:\n  [UNOSAT, FL20260826NPL](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/mudflow-rockflow-impact-assessment-in-rasuwa-nuwakot-districts-bagmati-province-nepal-as-o).\n\n**Carried over from the first map**\n\nThe channel, the three reaches with their measured bed gradients, and the\nmodelled population figures this map checks.\n[The first map and its methods](https://github.com/arjxn-py/nepal-flood-26-aug).\n\n**Imagery**\n\nThe before and after are Sentinel-2, 10 m, true colour, from the Copernicus\nprogramme, which is openly licensed. No single pass after the flood is usable —\nthey run 70 to 90% cloud — so each side is a median of the cloud-free pixels\nacross several passes, using the product's own per-pixel scene classification.\nGround that never had a clear look is left as a gap rather than filled in.\n\nThe agencies worked from much sharper pictures than this. The Copernicus grading\nwas interpreted from Pléiades Neo of 29 November 2025 and WorldView-3 of\n27 August 2026, both at 0.3 m; UNOSAT used CARTOSAT-3; HOT's model used SkySat.\nThose are commercial images, released inside the map products and reserved\notherwise, so the vectors derived from them can be redistributed here and the\nimages themselves cannot. The [EMSR927 products](https://mapping.emergency.copernicus.eu/activations/EMSR927/)\nare worth opening for that reason alone.\n\n**Checked and not used**\n\nA matched Sentinel-1 radar pair, 16 and 28 August, same orbit and pass. It\nregistered a strong change at about one site in eight of those later mapped\ndestroyed, and nothing distinguishable at the rest, so it is not shown as a\nlayer.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Sources"
        }
      }
